description:
"Public-site visual regression" failed on #2831 (run 37961549887, job 113945316700) and on #2823 with "Error: No unexpired protected public-site visual baseline is bound to base SHA 08cf03c5eb8a... or a site-equivalent ancestor" (results-explorer/scripts/download-public-site-visual-baseline.mjs:50). Among the 10 most recently merged PRs on 2026-10-09, 2 failed this way, 6 passed and 2 skipped. The base commits were fresh develop commits whose baseline had not been built yet, likely because the job that builds it was still queued (see actions-runner-queue-oracle-latency-20261009). The check is not required, so it does not block merges, but it teaches people to ignore a red check.

Investigate how and when the baseline for a develop commit is produced, and decide one of:
- fall back to the newest available ancestor baseline when none is bound to the base;
- wait for the baseline;
- report "baseline pending" as a neutral or skipped result instead of a failure.

Guardrails. Do not weaken the visual comparison itself. Related: astro-site-51-visual-gate-transition.
